cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, cite it as below. If you use the frozen Jira cache
  archive, cite the Zenodo deposit instead, once minted — see
  deposit/DEPOSIT_CHECKLIST.md.
title: >-
  Traceability and estimate coverage as corpus-eligibility constraints:
  a probe of 38 Apache projects
abstract: >-
  An independent pre-doctoral empirical study of what precedes a developer's
  decision to refactor. 38 Apache projects were probed against a pre-registered
  0.80 commit-side traceability bar; 12 passed and all 12 are Hadoop-ecosystem.
  The channel the literature publishes — what fraction of commits cite a ticket —
  diverges sharply from the one an issue-anchored study needs: what fraction of
  tickets ever receive a commit. The repository carries pre-registered
  predictions, six hypotheses that failed with named causes, a retracted Cox
  model, a self-corrected aggregation error, and a provenance row for every
  number.
